lean\\n- [x] `mise run test:ci` — unit + integration + canary green\\n- [x] Unit tests cover: passthrough, empty inputs, no-marker, marker-at-start, marker-in-repo-root, outside-base, traversal-rejection, worktree fallback\\n- [x] Integration test (`TestClaudeCode_WorktreePathFallback`) drives `entire hooks claude-code stop` with a fake HOME and a worktree-encoded `transcript_path` that doesn't exist; verifies a checkpoint is created end-to-end. Sanity-checked: with the resolver disabled the test fails with the exact error string from the field report.\\n- [ ] Manual: trigger a Claude Code session inside `.claude/worktrees/<branch>/`; confirm `entire status` shows the session and the next commit gets an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- Should also be reported upstream to Claude Code: `transcript_path` should match actual storage location.\\n- Logs an info-level message (`agent.claudecode resolved transcript via worktree fallback`) when the redirect fires, observable in `.entire/logs/`.\",\"number\":1159,\"title\":\"Fall back to scanning when Claude transcript_path is missing\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1159\"}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0b1d8a23-4f46-45bd-8254-efc987d65ed7","timestamp":"2026-05-11T13:43:52.287Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nFix dropped checkpoints when Claude Code runs from inside its `.claude/worktrees/<branch>/` feature.\\n\\nClaude reports `transcript_path` encoded from the worktree CWD, e.g.\\n`~/.claude/projects/-Users-foo-Development-repo--claude-worktrees-feature/<id>.jsonl`,\\nbut the file is actually written under the parent repo's project dir\\n`~/.claude/projects/-Users-foo-Development-repo/<id>.jsonl`. The TurnEnd handler aborted at the file-exists check, so no shadow-branch commit, no condense to `entire/checkpoints/v1`, and `prepare-commit-msg` had no checkpoint id to inject — user-visible symptom: commits land without an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer or proper agent attrib